uRowListHeight","shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rowListHeight"],"scenario":"real Qt 6 QML engine: rebuildDmenuDisplay() of 231 options at the head; count height passes and row visits (claimed fix: 1 pass / 231 visits; reproducer measures 232 / 27,027)"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The PR says to \"Bind visibleRowsHeight only to layoutSerial\" and gives \"walked_once 231\". In QML, a binding's dependencies are every property read while it evaluates, including reads inside called JS functions. rowListHeight (Menu.qml:206) and dmenuRowListHeight (Menu.qml:228) still loop `i < displayModel.count`, so count stays a dependency and each per-row append() (Menu.qml:628, :734) still re-runs the walk. The PR body itself says reads inside the walk \"remain binding dependencies\". The real-engine reproducer still reports the defect: report-reproducers.test.mjs expects exit 1 + 'DEFECT: 231-row menu open' and passed, and the KI evidence was refreshed at b09940a3 with known_issue_reproduced. Our manual qml6 differential (outside the package) measured 232 passes / 27,027 visits at base and at head. This is not a typed test outcome for the PR's purpose.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":228},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":734},{"id":"test/node/report-reproducers.test.mjs","kind":"test"},{"id":"test/reports/report-cmulr8ysi0jwr1gw4fjmt9khq.sh","kind":"file","line":1}],"severity":"high","title":"Question: does the PR remove the quadratic walk at all? The evidence says it does not","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Real-engine cost witness for menu open\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"menu-height-quadratic-test.sh regex-checks the Menu.qml binding and signatures, then asserts simulate(231,false).walked == 231 for a JS function it defines itself. It never evaluates the binding, so it passes while the real engine still walks 27,027 rows. I re-ran it at the evaluated commit: 13 ok lines, exit 0. On the mirror it runs (unmodified) inside menumodel-replay.test.mjs, which passed. That pass shows the source shape only, not the fix. Opinion: its assertion name 'menu height no longer scales with the square of row count' overstates what it checks.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","kind":"file","line":80},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1338},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"test"}],"severity":"medium","title":"The PR's own test pins source text and a JS simulation, not the QML engine","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"candidate":"unmapped_code|test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","path":"test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","position":"spec_gap"},"type":"unmapped_code"},"detail":"The behaviour this test targets (opening a menu costs O(n) height work) is intended: #10601 reports its absence and KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC's remediation says \"Also add a requirement that bounds the menu-open cost; none exists today\". B757 states only the fold geometry, not how often it is computed. Position spec_gap: add a requirement bounding height passes per rebuild (e.g. at most 2 walks per row). It needs a real-engine witness: the report reproducer's counter, not this source-text test. Then trace a corrected test to it. Tracing the PR's test as-is would codify a check that cannot fail on the defect.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC.yaml","kind":"file","line":23}],"severity":"medium","title":"Scope: the new test traces to no requirement, and no requirement bounds menu-open cost (spec_gap)","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"unmapped_code|test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","kind":"candidate"},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","kind":"file"}],"method":"review.scope (changed units, intent graph, spec-gap candidates): specGapCandidates","note":"The package flags unmapped_code|test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh (unmapped_code, severity medium): New file test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh is traced to no requirement: behaviour without intent. The author's position (spec_gap) is judgement, not verified; a human decision settles it.","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"Verified: base Menu.qml lines 231-236 (`// Implements: SW-REQ-260929-B8N9` + item()) are byte-identical to head lines 235-240. The PR adds 3 comment lines at 117-119 and 1 at 197 above it. The head claimEvidence for B8N9 carries the qualified record test:shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:237:item. The witness id moved, the behaviour did not. Not intended or unintended as behaviour: it is an id artefact of line-keyed witnesses. The auditor note (rdec-c345975b62261698da22e70120df5a07) is not an approval. compat_change_unapproved stays open until a human reviewer runs accept_compat_change.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":237},{"id":"SW-REQ-260929-B8N9","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Compat cf-c8dd4255b9f5771b: B8N9 witness Menu.qml:233:item gone at the head (in my reading a line shift; unapproved)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.behaviorDiff ran 213 inputs over corpus/data/lifecycle/scale/timing with 0 differences. Its harness (test/bdiff/harness.mjs) drives MenuModel.js JSONC parsing and the request lifecycle, never the visibleRowsHeight binding. Because the PR claims a performance change, the missing COST partition matters. Our manual qml6 differential (bdiff/10631.md, outside the package) found 0 height value differences and identical pass/visit counts on the headline input. Those results cannot be typed as behavior_changed claims.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120}],"severity":"medium","title":"The configured differential has no height or cost partition: 0 differences is no evidence for this change","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rowListHeight","shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"open a 20-row search with the divider shown, then cancel() and toggle searchDivider without a rebuild: compare visibleRowsHeight to a fresh rebuild"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The explicit args were dependency carriers. After the change, invalidation relies on reads inside the bodies: displayModel.count/get(i), root.filterText via rowHeightForDetail (only when count>0), root.mode, dmenuMaxHeight, and panel.height/cardTop/maxRowsHeight. searchDivider is truly dropped. Today it is written only inside rebuildDisplay, which then bumps layoutSerial (Menu.qml:735), and cancel() clears filterText without a rebuild (Menu.qml:906). Our manual run found no stale height. A future writer that toggles the divider without a rebuild would leave it stale.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":735},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":906},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: does any state change now leave a stale height, with searchDivider no longer a dependency?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Stale-height probe for no-rebuild state changes\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"Menu.qml:670-672. The PR says: \"When rebuildDisplay returns early because rows are not loaded, bump layoutSerial so the card collapses without relying on a count binding.\" It adds one binding evaluation with the same value (the base invalidated through count). It is harmless. It is also unnecessary for correctness while the bodies still read count.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":670},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"The new rowsLoaded=false serial bump is intended, and the PR states it","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Menu.qml:117-119 (\"Height must not bind to displayModel.count ... one pass is enough\") and :197 (\"_serial is a binding dependency only\") tell future maintainers the binding depends on layoutSerial alone. Reads inside the called functions are tracked, so the comments are inaccurate and may lead someone to assume the quadratic is fixed.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":117},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":197}],"severity":"low","title":"Opinion: the new code comments state a QML dependency model that does not hold","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"These requirements (including B757 for the changed functions) are verified by test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh and menu-acceptance-test.sh. Both need a live Hyprland/Quickshell session and are not in any audit suite. Their outcomes are unobserved at this revision, so these requirements are not tested here. The gap predates the PR. The disclosures still prevent readiness.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-4079","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-8CQ4","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-NM45","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260929-B8N9","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"10 test_outcome_unobserved disclosures: live compositor/acceptance tests are in no audit suite (baseline gap)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent for this QML change, so no new_call_path / reachable_from claims can be checked and uncodified connections cannot be detected. From reading the code: visibleRowsHeight feeds cardHeight only, and the height functions are called only from that binding. This is not engine-verified.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120}],"severity":"info","title":"Change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable): no QML effect/caller facts in the package","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:c05fb6b0afe30c17abac7f0ffb7195e6bfb4f5a47cb20dbe2b621bed7bfa89f7","packageIdentity":"epkg-7dd36f0463396852d3e979e0bf4823925e43577f6cafedd8451df5b16481e15a","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"Height values look unchanged: our manual qml6 differential found 0 value differences, but the package's own differential does not cover heights. The PR does not achieve its stated purpose: the quadratic open cost remains, and the KI reproducer still reports the defect. Its new test cannot detect that, and the inaccurate comments could mask it. One compatibility finding (a witness line shift) is unapproved. B757 and 9 other requirements have unobserved live-test outcomes. This is advisory only."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":2,"rationale":"Run the visibleRowsHeight binding + rebuildDmenuDisplay/rebuildDisplay in qml6 offscreen for 231 rows and assert height passes <= 2 and row visits <= 2n. Trace it to a new cost requirement. The KI reproducer's counter already does this; today it fails at head as well as at base.","refs":[{"id":"test/reports/report-cmulr8ysi0jwr1gw4fjmt9khq.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120}],"title":"Real-engine cost witness for menu open"},{"forClaim":7,"rationale":"For searchDivider toggles, cancel() filter clears, dmenuMaxHeight and panel geometry changes without a rebuild, assert visibleRowsHeight equals the value after a fresh rebuild.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120}],"title":"Stale-height probe for no-rebuild state changes"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #10631 (fresh3nough, fixes #10601) binds `visibleRowsHeight` to `rowListHeight(layoutSerial)` / `dmenuRowListHeight(layoutSerial)` and drops the `displayModel.count`, `filterText` and `searchDivider` args (Menu.qml:120). The `!rowsLoaded` early return now bumps `layoutSerial` (:670), and the PR adds test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh. Later mirror commits are our proof work, not upstream's: the PR test runs from menumodel-replay.test.mjs, plus a KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC note, an evidence refresh and a trace re-review.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** No, and the purpose is not achieved. QML tracks every property read during a binding's evaluation, including reads inside called functions. Both height functions still loop on `displayModel.count`, so each append still re-runs the walk. The real-engine KI reproducer still reports the defect: evidence was refreshed at b09940a3 as known_issue_reproduced, and report-reproducers.test.mjs passed expecting exit 1. Our manual qml6 differential (outside the package) found 232 passes / 27,027 row visits for 231 rows at both base and head, and 0 height value differences. The PR's own test passes (re-run here) but checks only source text and a JS simulation. Diff coverage has no changed decision lines.\n\n**Compatibility.** cf-c8dd4255b9f5771b is unapproved (prevents ready): the base B8N9 witness Menu.qml:233:item is gone at the head. item() is byte-identical and the witness sits at :237 after 4 added lines. I read it as a line shift. Only a human reviewer can approve it; the auditor note is not an approval. The configured differential (213 inputs, 0 differences) has no height or cost partition, so it is no evidence here.\n\n**Questions for a human.** Merge as a fix for #10601 when it does not remove the quadratic? Is implicit read tracking (searchDivider no longer a dependency) acceptable?\n\n**Traceability.** The changed functions trace to SW-REQ-260922-B757; 35 more requirements are code_changed via file-level traces. The new test traces to nothing. No requirement bounds menu-open cost, and KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC asks for one (spec_gap). effects_unavailable: change effects were not analyzed.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** 10 test_outcome_unobserved disclosures come from live Hyprland/Quickshell tests that are in no audit suite. Those requirements, B757 included, are not tested here. Readiness: not_assessed. Next decision: human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved)."}
